<launch>

  <!--
    Team Xiao Hei — object reference (Task 2), answered by Claude.

    The alternative to `scene_gemini.launch` for OBJECT_REFERENCE questions.
    Both bring up the same perception sidecar and build the same scene graph;
    they differ in how the robot moves and who answers:

      scene_gemini   frontier exploration sweeps the whole scene, then Gemini
                     answers from whatever the sweep collected.
      scene_claude   the `nav_task1` explorer drives *toward the object the
                     question names* — the model is shown the question plus the
                     objects detected so far on every reach / skip event, and
                     declares ARRIVED when it is there — then Claude picks the
                     referenced `object_id` out of the built graph.

    Two processes, same as scene_gemini:

      1. Perception sidecar — YOLO-World v2 + SAM 2.1 over HTTP on
         localhost:8001, in its own venv (/opt/perc-venv) so its numpy 2 /
         torch stack stays clear of the ROS 2 (numpy 1.26) Python.
      2. scene_claude node  — blocks on the sidecar's /healthz before it starts,
         so no ordering or delay is needed here.

    Requires ANTHROPIC_API_KEY — the same key the instruction-following stack
    uses. Without it the node raises at boot rather than ten minutes in.

    Selection is by environment, set here so the launch file is the whole
    contract and the image does not have to be rebuilt to switch pipelines:
    XIAO_HEI_RESPONDER=scene_claude picks the answerer, and
    XIAO_HEI_EXPLORATION_STRATEGY=nav_task1 picks the question-directed
    explorer. Setting one without the other is a misconfiguration — the
    responder would wait for an explorer that never completes, or the explorer
    would drive to the object and hand off to Gemini.
  -->

  <executable
      cmd="/opt/perc-venv/bin/python -m uvicorn perception.server:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8001"
      name="perception_sidecar"
      cwd="/opt"
      output="screen" />

  <executable
      cmd="xiao-hei-vlm"
      name="xiao_hei_scene_claude"
      output="screen">
    <env name="XIAO_HEI_RESPONDER" value="scene_claude" />
    <env name="XIAO_HEI_EXPLORATION_STRATEGY" value="nav_task1" />
  </executable>

</launch>
